{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 19, :comments [{:quotes [{:he "המסות הגדולות", :translit "ha-masot ha-gedolot", :gloss "the great trials"} {:he "כל האלפא ביתא בזה הפסוק חוץ מבי\"ת", :translit "kol ha-alpha beta ba-zeh ha-pasuk chutz mi-bet", :gloss "the entire alphabet is in this verse except for bet"} {:he "רמז כי עוד יעשה פעם שנית נפלאות", :translit "remez ki od ya'aseh pa'am shenit nifla'ot", :gloss "a sign that He will yet perform a second time wonders"} {:he "כימי צאתך מארץ מצרים", :translit "kimei tzeitkha me-eretz mitzrayim", :gloss "like the days of your going out from the land of Egypt"}], :mechanisms [{:kind :other, :note "Verse contains every letter of the alphabet except bet; bet's absence is itself the sign"}], :frame {:text "Isaiah 11:11 states that God will again recover the remnant of His people 'a second time,' and Micah 7:15 promises, 'As in the days of your coming out of the land of Egypt, I will show him wondrous things.' The word for 'second' (שנית) begins with shin, not bet; Ba'al HaTurim connects bet's absence to the numerical value of בראשית = 913, matching עוד יעשה פעם שנית, signaling that the wonders of the Exodus will be repeated.", :sources ["Isaiah 11:11" "Micah 7:15"]}}], :arithmetic [{:kind :other, :note "Verse contains every letter of the alphabet except bet; bet's absence is itself the sign", :by :selah, :ran? false}], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :baal-haturim, :lang :en, :chapter 7, :discipline "bht-chalkboard-v1", :timestamp "2026-07-12T23:35:03.083300180Z", :model "glm-5.2"}